[Q1] in_proj_qkv.weight shape = (6144, 1024)
  torch.split(mixed_qkv, [key_dim, key_dim, value_dim]) with key_dim=2048 value_dim=2048
  -> CONTIGUOUS BLOCKS: [0:2048]=Q, [2048:4096]=K, [4096:6144]=V. NOT interleaved.
  key_dim = head_k_dim*num_k_heads = 128*16 = 2048 (line 512); conv_dim = 2*key_dim+value_dim = 6144 (line 521)

[Q2] conv1d.weight shape = (6144, 1, 4)  bias = absent (bias=False, line 525)
  kernel_size = linear_conv_kernel_dim = 4  groups = channels = 6144 (depthwise), padding = K-1 = 3
  activation = config.hidden_act = silu (passed as activation=self.activation, line 594)
  padding=K-1 in F.conv1d is LEFT padding;  max|left_pad - ref_pad| = 1.1920928955078125e-07
  => silu is applied IMMEDIATELY after conv (activation passed into causal_conv1d_fn,
     which does ACT2FN[activation](out) at line 287-288), BEFORE the Q/K/V split.

[Q5] linear_num_k_heads = 16  linear_num_v_heads = 16  -> num_v_heads // num_k_heads = 1
  condition `if self.num_v_heads // self.num_k_heads > 1` (line 620) is FALSE -> repeat_interleave NOT executed for this model

[Q4c] F.softplus(a.float() + dt_bias) -- torch default beta=1.0, threshold=20.0
  (a+dt_bias) range: [-13.2146, 8.4654]  -> max 8.4654 < 20, so the threshold branch is NEVER taken
  softplus == log1p(exp(x)) here: max|softplus - log1p(exp(x))| = 3.725290298461914e-09
  manual log1p(exp()) vs torch, max|diff| = 3.725290298461914e-09

[Q4b/Q8] g = -exp(A_log) * softplus(a + dt_bias)  (line 619)
  g        range: [-6.735915, -0.000000]   (must be <= 0)
  gamma=exp(g) range: [0.00118749, 1.00000000]  -> strictly inside (0,1): False
  per-token gamma mean = 0.764758
  gamma shape = (5, 16)  = [batch, seq, num_v_heads] -> ONE SCALAR PER (token, v-head), shared over k-dim
  => the decay is NOT per-k-channel; a single scalar multiplies the whole [k_dim,v_dim] state

[Q3] l2norm (modeling_qwen3_5.py:294-297):
   inv_norm = torch.rsqrt((x*x).sum(dim=-1,keepdim=True) + eps); return x * inv_norm
   eps = 1e-6, hard-coded at the call sites (lines 344-345 / 464-465), i.e. rsqrt(sum+1e-6) form.
   q is THEN scaled: query = query / (query.shape[-1] ** 0.5)  (line 468), head_k_dim=128 -> /sqrt(128)

[Q6] Qwen3_5RMSNormGated (line 218-234), weight shape = (128,) == head_v_dim (per-head, ONE shared vector of length head_v_dim)
   weight stats mean=0.95163 std=0.08585 min=0.52344 max=1.05957  (init ones, so NOT zero-centred: line 221 vs Qwen3_5RMSNorm line 845 which is zeros/(1+w))
   ORDER (lines 228-232): variance = mean(x^2) over the LAST dim (head_v_dim);
                          x = x * rsqrt(variance + eps);  x = weight * x;
                          x = x * silu(gate)   <-- NORM FIRST, THEN gate
   eps = config.rms_norm_eps = 1e-06

[Q12] q_norm/k_norm are applied BEFORE RoPE: lines 792-797 --
      query_states = self.q_norm(query_states.view(hidden_shape)).transpose(1,2)
      key_states   = self.k_norm(self.k_proj(hidden_states).view(hidden_shape)).transpose(1,2)
      ... then apply_rotary_pos_emb(query_states, key_states, cos, sin)  (line 797)
      both norms have weight shape [256] == head_dim (config head_dim=256, rms_norm_eps=1e-6)

[Q13] scaling = head_dim**-0.5 = 0.06250000 (line 758, head_dim=256)
      num_key_value_groups = 8//2 = 4
      repeat_kv (line 712-721): [b, nkv, s, hd] -> [:, :, None].expand(b, nkv, n_rep, s, hd)
      -> reshape(b, nkv*n_rep, s, hd).  Because the expanded axis ORDER is (nkv, n_rep),
      flattened head index h maps to kv head  kv = h // n_rep  (equivalently h // groups).

